# nginx.conf's rewrites as real 301s (astro.config.mjs's redirects only write meta-refresh pages).
# Each path is listed with and without its trailing slash, and each old URL reaches its page in one hop.
#
# Order matters. Cloudflare checks exact paths first, but only the ones above the first line with a
# placeholder (:name) or a splat (*). Every line after that is a pattern, and the live site does not keep
# the patterns in file order: /en/* won over /en/pathways/:name and /en/support/about. So every exact
# path stays in the first block, the old /en/ Pathway pages are listed one by one, and no two patterns
# below match the same URL.

